[00:49.12] Beyond the horizon of the place we lived when we were young
[00:55.82] In a world of magnets and miracles
[01:01.40] Our thoughts strayed constantly and without boundary
[01:08.14] The ringing of the division bell had begun
[01:14.55] Along the Long Road and on down the causeway
[01:21.50] Do they still meet there by the Cut?
[01:27.92] There was a ragged band that followed in our footsteps
[01:34.12] Running before time took our dreams away
[01:40.26] Leaving the myriad small creatures trying to tie us to the ground
[01:46.92] To a life consumed by slow decay
[01:52.07] The grass was greener
[01:55.93] 
[01:58.11] The light was brighter
[02:02.25] 
[02:05.99] With friends surrounded
[02:11.86] The nights of wonder
[02:15.99] 
[02:19.68] Looking beyond the embers of bridges glowing behind us
[02:26.40] To a glimpse of how green it was on the other side
[02:32.75] Steps taken forwards, but sleepwalking back again
[02:38.95] Dragged by the force of some inner tide
[02:45.34] At a higher altitude with flag unfurled
[02:52.05] We reached the dizzy heights of that dreamed of world
[02:58.70] 
[04:02.14] Encumbered forever by desire and ambition
[04:08.69] There's a hunger still unsatisfied
[04:14.74] Our weary eyes still stray to the horizon
[04:21.12] Though down this road we've been so many times
[04:26.87] The grass was greener
[04:32.73] The light was brighter
[04:37.12] 
[04:39.33] The taste was sweeter
[04:43.28] 
[04:45.55] The nights of wonder
[04:49.88] 
[04:51.96] With friends surrounded
[04:56.18] 
[04:58.37] The dawn mist glowing
[05:04.09] The water flowing
[05:07.97] 
[05:10.78] The endless river
[05:14.71] 
[05:16.83] Forever and ever
